 "role": "negative_bw",
 "balance": "daylight",
 "source": "HARMAN technology Limited, ILFORD XP2 SUPER Technical Information (Nov 2018); curves traced from the PDF's raster chart images (spectral page 2, characteristic curve page 3)",
 "notes": "Approximate digitization; not supplied or endorsed by HARMAN technology. Both charts are embedded raster images (no vector curve paths); the characteristic curve was traced at native resolution from column-wise darkness peaks (columns on vertical grid lines and peaks on horizontal grid lines skipped and bridged by interpolation), the spectral curve with a centreline follower after thin grid and frame lines were removed by a 3x3 grey opening; axes calibrated on the printed grid lines and tick marks. The characteristic-curve image is small (292 x 210 px, about 27 px per 0.5 D), so expect about +-0.02 D / +-0.02 log E reading uncertainty. Characteristic curve (page 3): the datasheet prints a single curve, 'processed through standard C41 type chemicals', representative of 35mm and roll film; XP2 SUPER is a chromogenic (dye-image) film and push processing is not recommended, so no other development is charted and all_curves holds only this curve. x is the chart's own 'Relative log exposure' axis (labels 1-4, arbitrary origin), not log H in lux-seconds; density axis labelled 1.0 and 2.0, zero taken at the bottom grid line by the equal grid spacing; the chart does not state the densitometry (visual, Status M or other). Tracing noise in the flat toe was removed with a running maximum so density is non-decreasing. log_h_ref: none. The chart carries no 18% grey, speed-point or normal-exposure mark; the text gives ISO 400/27 to daylight measured with standard C41 processing, a usable range EI 50/18-800/30 and says the recommended EI is a practical evaluation, not ISO foot speed, so no reference exposure is placed on the relative axis. Spectral sensitivity (page 2): 'Wedge spectrogram to tungsten light (2856K)'; the vertical axis is labelled 'Sensitivity' with only two ticks, 0.5 and 1.0, and no statement whether it is linear or logarithmic; values are read on that tick scale as charted (linear between and beyond the ticks), so the curve ends where it meets the chart's bottom frame, which lies at 0.00 on that scale. No granularity, RMS granularity, MTF or contrast-time data are published in this datasheet; rms_granularity is therefore omitted. Not recorded (no field in this schema): reciprocity formula Ta = Tm^1.31 for exposures over 1 s.",
